2026-08-14: Measured evaluator mechanics, split sizes, seed uniqueness, origin volumes, label rates, study types, phases, trial ages, enrollment distributions, and title/summary/description availability without accessing test labels.
2026-08-14: Copied the champion implementation without prediction artifacts and removed active obsolete-run restoration. Added a cache-first staged orchestrator, namespaced core/invariant/registry/literature artifacts, SHA-pinned AACT snapshot materialization, physical Model-A freezes, and final checksum checks.
2026-08-14: Implemented literature v3 PubMed SI plus literal-verified TIAB retrieval, Europe PMC accession plus literal-verified quoted/full-text retrieval, point-in-time AACT RESULT PMIDs, strictly version-dated preprints, multi-identifier deduplication, eight-paper filtering, safe fullTextXML section windows, extended hosted adjudication, confidence-tiered nonnegative routing, 2018 selection, sealed-2019 confirmation, and component diagnostics.
2026-08-14: External publication provenance uses NCBI E-utilities and Europe PMC REST APIs. Every query is origin-censored; each document independently requires a complete pre-origin first/electronic/version date or an earlier year for non-preprints, while corrections, retractions, expressions of concern, post-origin versions, citation counts, and current registry summaries are rejected. Full text requires a matching PMCID-specific XML article, complete pre-origin publication date, and no later version/correction marker.
2026-08-14: Full evaluation attempt 1 failed after the core completed because the SHA-pinned AACT download is a ZIP container and was passed directly to `pg_restore`, which reported `input file does not appear to be a valid archive`. Added atomic extraction of `postgres_data.dmp`, retained the outer archive SHA pin in projection metadata, and made the completed core cache resumable so the retry does not repeat hosted work.
2026-08-14: Full evaluation attempt 2 failed at the 2018-06-01 SHA check because the champion changes log supplied a 65-character digest ending `...d69c`; SHA-256 digests are 64 characters and the downloaded archive independently hashed to its exact 64-character prefix ending `...d69`. Corrected that one malformed pin after verifying the other five supplied pins are each 64 characters.
2026-08-14: Publication preflight found that a few Europe PMC quoted searches broadened to 1,000 metadata hits, causing the initial implementation to attempt full-text literal verification for every non-metadata match. Narrow-result queries still verify metadata or full text, but broad expansions now reject non-metadata matches; this preserves precision and restored bounded retrieval work.
2026-08-14: The first interrupted publication preflight remained alive as PID 1674857 after its PTY returned; it was explicitly terminated and marked abandoned. A second interrupted verifier PID 1675560 was likewise terminated before restart. Full-text literal verification was tightened from at most 50 to at most five search hits because broader sets are not sufficiently specific for conservative trial linkage.
2026-08-14: A third publication preflight worker PID 1676264 was explicitly terminated after successful full-text-verification cache growth stalled: non-OA PMCID checks were consuming the general six-retry network policy. Optional literal-verification full-text fetches now attempt once and conservatively reject failures; selected safe candidate documents retain six retries.
2026-08-14: Full-text hydration then exposed the same issue on a selected PMCID with a deterministic HTTP 404. The common retriever now fails fast on non-429 HTTP 4xx responses while retaining six exponential-backoff retries for transient errors; unavailable full text immediately falls back to the pre-origin abstract.
